    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x^4}{x^{-2}}\\times x^{-7}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac1x$, $x\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "The original expression requires $x\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^4}{x^{-2}}\\times x^{-7}&=x^{4-(-2)-7}\\\\\\frac{x^4}{x^{-2}}\\times x^{-7}&=x^{-1}\\\\\\frac{x^4}{x^{-2}}\\times x^{-7}&=\\frac1x.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q2-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(a^3b^{-2})^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\times(a^{-1}b)^{\\frac{3}{2}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt b$, $a>0$, $b>0$.\n\nMultiply the indices within each bracket, then collect powers of each base.",
          "worked": "For real values, the original expression requires $a\\ne0$ and $b\\ne0$. Its first square root requires $a>0$; the second fractional power then requires $b>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(a^3b^{-2})^{\\frac{1}{2}}(a^{-1}b)^{\\frac{3}{2}}&=a^{\\frac{3}{2}}b^{-1}a^{-\\frac{3}{2}}b^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\\\(a^3b^{-2})^{\\frac{1}{2}}(a^{-1}b)^{\\frac{3}{2}}&=a^0b^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\\\(a^3b^{-2})^{\\frac{1}{2}}(a^{-1}b)^{\\frac{3}{2}}&=\\sqrt b.\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $a>0$, $b>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q3-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt[3]{x^5}\\times\\sqrt x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^{\\frac{13}{6}}$, $x\\ge0$.",
          "worked": "The square root requires $x\\ge0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt[3]{x^5}\\times\\sqrt x&=x^{\\frac{5}{3}}x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\\\\\sqrt[3]{x^5}\\times\\sqrt x&=x^{\\frac{10}{6}+\\frac{3}{6}}\\\\\\sqrt[3]{x^5}\\times\\sqrt x&=x^{\\frac{13}{6}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q4-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1{\\sqrt[3]{8x^2y^4}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac1{2x^{\\frac{2}{3}}y^{\\frac{4}{3}}}$, $x\\ne0$, $y\\ne0$, using real cube roots.",
          "worked": "The denominator is nonzero when $x\\ne0$ and $y\\ne0$. Interpret powers with denominator 3 using real cube roots.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{\\sqrt[3]{8x^2y^4}}&=\\frac1{\\sqrt[3]8\\,\\sqrt[3]{x^2}\\,\\sqrt[3]{y^4}}\\\\\\frac1{\\sqrt[3]{8x^2y^4}}&=\\frac1{2x^{\\frac{2}{3}}y^{\\frac{4}{3}}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
